WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.320
You gave an agent permission to pay.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.741
Then you revoked that permission.

00:00:06.741 --> 00:00:10.701
Can an approval issued earlier still spend your funds?

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:15.982
ProofPass combines private authorization with execution-time revocation.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.842
This demo shows a recorded testnet run.

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:22.778
First, the private policy.

00:00:22.778 --> 00:00:29.181
Identity details and the full delegation limit stay off the destination chain.

00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:34.354
The public request identifies the agent, recipient, and amount.

00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:44.205
Midnight checks identity evidence from the Open D I D SDK, credential status, wallet binding, and delegation conditions.

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.596
Here is why zero knowledge matters.

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:55.142
The proof shows that zero point zero five SOL is within a hidden per-transaction limit.

00:00:55.142 --> 00:01:00.033
The demo discloses a limit of zero point one SOL for explanation.

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:05.450
A request for zero point one five fails before authorization is created.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.977
Now, an actual payment.

00:01:08.977 --> 00:01:14.229
A trusted relay registers the request-bound authorization on Solana.

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:21.181
The program checks the request, current state, expiry, and whether the approval is unused.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:25.816
Fifty million lamports move from the vault to the recipient.

00:01:25.816 --> 00:01:28.751
That is zero point zero five test SOL.

00:01:30.587 --> 00:01:32.606
Here is the critical case.

00:01:32.606 --> 00:01:36.332
A separate, unused authorization already exists.

00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:42.544
Then the X R P L credential is deleted, and the observer updates Solana's state.

00:01:42.544 --> 00:01:47.979
Executing the old approval fails with source error six thousand three.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:51.162
About seven seconds remain before expiry.

00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:54.967
Authority was revoked, so the payment is blocked.

00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:58.538
No funds move from the vault to the recipient.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.301
Compare all four outcomes.

00:02:02.301 --> 00:02:04.123
A valid request is paid.

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:07.007
Reusing the same approval is rejected.

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:10.347
Revoking the mandate blocks an old approval.

00:02:10.347 --> 00:02:16.647
Deleting the credential also blocks an old approval once the update reaches Solana.

00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:22.036
Both successful payments and rejected attempts have execution evidence.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:26.452
The trust boundaries are explicit.

00:02:26.452 --> 00:02:30.195
Solana does not verify Midnight proofs directly.

00:02:30.195 --> 00:02:35.498
The system trusts adapters, a relay, an observer, and supplied time.

00:02:35.498 --> 00:02:42.048
Revocation propagation takes time, and enforcement covers this vault's payment path.

00:02:42.048 --> 00:02:45.947
Corporate agent delegation is a future experiment.

00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:48.052
Prove permission privately.

00:02:48.052 --> 00:02:49.923
Enforce it at execution.
